# NVIDIA's open nouveau driver for a card before Turing (GeForce GTX 10xx, Quadro Pxxx, Pascal:
# GP102 to GP108), with the display and HDMI sound built in: /dev/dri/card* and renderD* for a
# workload that claims them, and /dev/snd for the sound of the screen. Nouveau's display and
# HDMI sound work on any NVIDIA card before Turing it knows; the firmware below gives 3D
# (OpenGL) on a desktop Pascal card, GP102 to GP108. There is no reclocking (the card stays at
# its boot clock) and no video decode under nouveau; NVIDIA's own driver is not part of kith OS.
# Built in, not modules, so the root stays the plain image's size and a node installed from a
# plain image takes the update. (The HDMI codec of NVIDIA's cards is on by default with the
# option below, as the Kconfig of 6.18 has it.)
# pci: 10de:1b00 10de:1b01 10de:1b02 10de:1b04 10de:1b06 10de:1b07 10de:1b30 10de:1b38 10de:1b39 10de:1b70 10de:1b78
# pci: 10de:1b80 10de:1b81 10de:1b82 10de:1b83 10de:1b84 10de:1b87 10de:1ba0 10de:1ba1 10de:1ba2 10de:1ba9 10de:1baa
# pci: 10de:1bad 10de:1bb0 10de:1bb1 10de:1bb3 10de:1bb4 10de:1bb5 10de:1bb6 10de:1bb7 10de:1bb8 10de:1bb9 10de:1bbb
# pci: 10de:1bc7 10de:1be0 10de:1be1 10de:1c00 10de:1c01 10de:1c02 10de:1c03 10de:1c04 10de:1c06 10de:1c07 10de:1c09
# pci: 10de:1c20 10de:1c21 10de:1c22 10de:1c23 10de:1c2d 10de:1c30 10de:1c31 10de:1c35 10de:1c36 10de:1c60 10de:1c61
# pci: 10de:1c62 10de:1c70 10de:1c81 10de:1c82 10de:1c83 10de:1c8c 10de:1c8d 10de:1c8e 10de:1c8f 10de:1c90 10de:1c91
# pci: 10de:1c92 10de:1c94 10de:1c96 10de:1ca7 10de:1ca8 10de:1caa 10de:1cb1 10de:1cb2 10de:1cb3 10de:1cb6 10de:1cba
# pci: 10de:1cbb 10de:1cbc 10de:1cbd 10de:1ccc 10de:1ccd 10de:1cfa 10de:1cfb 10de:1d01 10de:1d02 10de:1d10 10de:1d11
# pci: 10de:1d12 10de:1d13 10de:1d16 10de:1d33 10de:1d34 10de:1d52 10de:1d56
CONFIG_DRM_NOUVEAU=y
CONFIG_SOUND=y
CONFIG_SND=y
CONFIG_SND_PCI=y
CONFIG_SND_HDA_INTEL=y
CONFIG_SND_HDA_CODEC_HDMI=y
# firmware: nvidia/gp102/*/* nvidia/gp104/*/* nvidia/gp106/*/* nvidia/gp107/*/* nvidia/gp108/*/*
